#!/bin/zsh
# Fetches the worker's macOS arm64 binary from kyrios/encode-queue's release into
# build/worker/encode-worker (docs/worker.md). Without that release it says so and exits 0:
# the app then runs ProRes only.
#   bin/fetch-worker [tag]    default v0.1.0
set -euo pipefail
cd "${0:A:h}/.."
tag=${1:-v0.1.0}
repo=kyrios/encode-queue
mkdir -p build/worker
rm -f build/worker/*
if ! gh release view "$tag" -R $repo >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  print "no release $tag of $repo yet: building without the worker"
  exit 0
fi
gh release download "$tag" -R $repo -D build/worker -p '*darwin*arm64*' -p 'SHA256SUMS*' -p '*checksums*'
cd build/worker
for sums in SHA256SUMS* *checksums*(N); do
  [[ -f $sums ]] && shasum -a 256 -c --ignore-missing "$sums"
done
bin=$(ls | grep -E 'darwin.*arm64' | head -1)
case $bin in
  *.tar.gz) tar xzf "$bin"; bin=$(find . -type f -name 'encode-worker*' ! -name '*.tar.gz' | head -1) ;;
  *.zip) ditto -x -k "$bin" .; bin=$(find . -type f -name 'encode-worker*' ! -name '*.zip' | head -1) ;;
esac
mv "$bin" encode-worker
chmod +x encode-worker
file encode-worker | grep -q 'Mach-O 64-bit executable arm64'
./encode-worker --version || true
